ll-up R11) appears to be on this junction, which would tie SDA to GND.\",\n      \"expected\": \"SDA (D1, tied to D2) should be a separate bus line pulled up by R11. Only unused data pins should be tied to GND, and they should not be joined to the SDA line.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"`DISP_SDA`: U2 pin 35 (`PB14`) \u2014 R7 (10 k\u03a9) to VCC \u2014 U4 pins 19/20 (`D1`/`D2`)\"},\n        {\"source\": \"schematic\", \"quote\": \"display.kicad_sch (page 3): D1 wire at y\u2248444 with junction at x\u2248741 joining the vertical bus down to the GND symbol, and NET0012 taken from the D1 line via R11\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the junction is real, SDA is shorted to GND. The display would not respond on I2C, and the pull-up R11 would fight the ground connection.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.35\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The NFC I2C lines are crossed across the sheet boundary: PB9 (pin 62) drives the NTAG SCL pin and PB8 (pin 61) drives its SDA pin, contrary to the specification. A possible second issue is the display data bus, where the SDA branch appears to join a GND bus at x\u2248741.\"\n}",
